%N A123405 Number of alternately orientable perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123405 A graph is alternately orientable if its edges can be oriented so that the directions alternate around every chordless cycle of length at least 4. Every alternately orientable graph is perfect. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Sep 28 2026
